0  but as well as that learning and  development that will undertake it that  will be undertaken  within the their employment will also  count towards their 20  of their off the job learning so  training and development that assists  them to develop and grow within their  role within the organization  is completely valid as far as that 20  allocation is concerned  so if they're taking part in shadowing  and mentoring within the workplace and  it's supporting them to develop new  knowledge skills and behaviors  within their role that counts towards  the 20  if for argument's sake an individual is  within  a sales team within the organization  and they have the opportunity to attend  a finance meeting to get a better  understanding  of the relationship between finance and  sales in the organization and how that  team operates  that's completely valid as part of  developing that individual and counting  towards their 20  so the key tests really in terms of  what's valid and eligible as far as the  20  is concerned is is the time spent within  their normal working hours  is the individual undertaking training  and development that can support them in  their knowledge and understanding of  their role  and are they learning new knowledge  skills and behaviors  if those three tests are met it's valid  and eligible as far as that 20  off the job learning is concerned and i  do apologize about my dog now just  getting angry and aggressive and barking  in the background somewhere  thank you andy so in terms of the  support infrastructure then  around both the university and the  employer for apprenticeships  first and foremost every individual  needs to be allocated a work based  mentor  there's a couple of different uh thought  processes on that  some organizations are happy for the  line manager to be the work based mentor  because of the proximity to the student  and the role  and those kinds of things um other  organizations prefer that  the work based mentor is not the line  manager and the principle behind that  really is that the  mentor then not being the line manager  can give the individual  accessibility to other parts of the  organization that they wouldn't  necessarily  be engaged with on a normal day-to-day  basis  within the university we have the  programme lead in this particular case  for the management apprenticeships  that's myself  i'm always accessible and available to  students employers line managers and  mentors  and the first point of contact generally  is the module tutor and the personal  tutor  but everybody has accessibility to my  details and i can be  contacted for really whatever support is  required around  the programs uh every module that we run  has a module tutor clearly and the  module tutor is a subject-specific  expert  in that subject and they are the first  point of contact  in relation to queries and questions  relating to the subject knowledge and  area  they also support all of the online  study materials during that period  every student has allocated a personal  tutor and  our ideal scenario and it does tend to  or it has tended to work so far  our ideal scenario is that the personal  tutor is allocated to the individual and  is with the individual  for the duration of their program the  benefit to that really is that it gives  the personal tutor and the apprentice  the opportunity to really get to know  each other well  you get to understand each other's  working style the approach to the  apprenticeship  and also from the personal tutors  perspective they really get to  understand the individual's job and can  provide the best possible advice  in terms of how to gather and pull  together evidence that presents that  student in the best possible right as  far as  the portfolio of evidence is concerned  we have a team of online learning  advisors the online learning advisors  will support across  all sorts of queries and questions  anything really from  um you know i've been under  a lot of pressure at work and i need an  extension of my deadline for this  particular piece of coursework  right through to i'm having financial  problems and i need to contact wellbeing  support and get some advice  in terms of finance support  and the well-being facilities within the  university are pretty immense if i'm  completely  honest ranging from everything from a gp  practice  through to support advice and guidance  on  mental health finance addiction  just every possible thing that you can  think of really  we have a full it function that will  support with all of the technology  accessibility  um and that will incorporate things like  ensuring that students have  accessibility to  the systems that they have a username  and a logon that they  have their university email address set  up  and that they know how to function and  access those and then also the library  facility  and the library facility again to a  certain degree is multifaceted in the  sense that we have  numerous physical library resources  across the different campuses  but also because of the nature of the  apprenticeship programs we try to ensure  that  the reading materials that we recommend  are accessible as e-resources through  the library  because that means that they're  available 24 hours a day seven days a  week  and it it gives the students the  opportunity to study them  at the best possible time that suits  them so if they're if their window in  the day is that they're working full  time they come home in the evening they  want some family time  to have a meal and to have some time  with kids for argument's sake and they  start studying from nine o'clock at  night until 11 o'clock at night  that suits them best we want to be sure  that they have accessibility to the  materials  at that time and that's why we uh we  tend to  utilize the uh the e-library facilities  as much as possible  and i think i i think there's something  like 50 000 books  available through the e-library  facilities um  so it's pretty comprehensive the  university is also  a member of a network uh called schonel  and schonel is 180 190  university and british libraries across  the uk and with  utilization of the university of derby's  id card  students can access any of those  universities  access books within those universities  and access study space within those  universities  so thinking about locations within  northeast derbyshire  if there is a university closer to where  somebody actually  lives they can attend that library and  utilize the library facilities  at the uh at their local university  rather than feeling they need to  have to make their way down into derby  city centre to be able to utilise the  university of derby campus facilities  thank you andy  oh sorry i'm looking at the wrong screen  didn't realize it moved on  and finally just the process then the  management apprenticeships are  fully fundable through the apprentice  apprenticeship levy scheme  as part of the program students either  have to produce at the  the outset of the program or achieve  during the program  the equivalent of functional skills  level 2 in maths english or a gcse grade  c  if students are able to provide that  certification  we can file that they don't need to do  matter english again  if they can't they will need to  undertake maths in english and there are  i know a number of adult community  learning schemes that they can utilize  for that  but they can also undertake their math  in english at the university of derby as  part of this particular program  as well now unfortunately that also  means  that we are only as i say this is  mandated  by the government as part of the  apprenticeship scheme we are only  allowed to give a buy on the maths in  english  if you can produce physical evidence  that you have those certificate  certificates in place  so unfortunately if you did your gcse  maths in english 25 years ago and you  can't find those certificates and you  can't re