d  in agreement so thank you very much  that's all i have for this morning  my details are there and again uh we've  mentioned to uh to maria that we're more  than happy for the  slides to be shared so uh my details  there and these details are there  if you do have any questions or queries  following up from this and  once you've had a chance to reflect on  what we've spoken about this morning  please do get in touch  thank you thanks verge  thank you thank you very much andy and  spencer that was absolutely amazing to  to see and hear and it's i'm very happy  that we get to  spread a bit awareness about these  apprenticeship but about the wide  variety  that there is about the wonderful  support and the absolutely  like amazingly flexible delivery of  these these apprenticeships and  now actually um to tell us about the  benefits of handling apprenticeships  from the business side  from the business perspective we have  lee barnes managing director  at inspire design so uh lee over to you  hello good morning i'm lee barnes  managing director of inspired design and  development  and i just want to talk a little bit  this morning  about how my business has benefited  from using the apprenticeship scheme  we are consulting engineers based in  play cross  we specialize in the delivery of  infrastructure for new development sites  of which north east derbyshire has  plenty currently  um we employ engineers and technicians  varying levels  as well as town and country planners and  of course the back office staff required  to deliver a successful business  as a small practice um competing  in the employment market against much  larger often  international consultancies can be a  real challenge for us  um geographically we're competing with  practices from  sheffield nottingham and derby and  there's a lot of competition there in  those cities  we have managed to successfully recruit  a candidate  creating the opportunities for that team  member  to advance their knowledge and  experience is key to helping them  fulfill  not only their potential but achieve  their own personal goals  but training team members is a  expensive undertaking there's the cost  of the course  the cost of the time off the loss of  productivity  well that's one way of looking at it  anyway we prefer to see it as an  investment  in the business it's an investment in  the future of the business an  investment in the future of our team and  to quote  sir richard branson train people well  enough  so they can leave treat them well enough  so they don't want to  that's what we try and do here  so providing opportunities for people to  grow and advance  helps to provide fulfillment and  satisfaction within their roles  to assist in upskilling the team we  utilize the  apprenticeship scheme extensively at all  levels but the area  where we're seeing the greatest impact  on the business is where we have people  undertaking degree level apprenticeships  and we currently have two undertaking  degree level  apprenticeships out of the team of 10 we  have an aspiring engineer  who joined us with a hnc qualification  and a good amount of practical  experience as well said  upon joining us we identified him as  having a high degree of  potential to move on within his career  although he did like a little bit of  confidence  we spoke to him about his career  aspirations and we set him up on the  civil engineering  degree program with the university of  derby as  andy previously mentioned since then  we've noticed  a marked difference in how he operates  within the business  he has become more confident his  knowledge base is broadened  and he started to become a really good  role model and mentor for the younger  team members  the course also offers a direct route  to achieving a professional  qualification through the institution of  civil engineers  which would be a significant industry  recognize benchmark  that is not only a feather in the camp  for the candidate himsel