rows and for  them to benefit from that by becoming  well  qualified confident professionals  it's helped me provide opportunities to  team members that  hadn't had one for one reason or another  or did not have the opportunity to go  into education higher education  previously  my passion to provide opportunity to  those who previously  hadn't had access to a degree course  stems from my own experience  i didn't enter the industry by the  traditional route of  doing a levels and then a full-time  degree course  i did a vtec qualification at  chesterfield college  a long time ago now longer than a  kettlebell  and then i managed to get a job at  derbyshire county councils  after after eight years or so of working  i decided to advance my career  and i was able to start a part-time  degree whilst working freelance  again not everybody else has the  opportunity to fund that themselves  rather  or they're freelancing so the  degree level apprenticeship route  provides that pathway to a professional  career for people  who maybe don't have the opportunity for  whatever reason whether that be social  or economic  or some people just don't mature  academically until later in life i  certainly fit that description  so in summary from my perspective as a  business owner  and as someone who is passionate about  providing alternative pathways to a  professional career  in civil engineering higher and degree  level apprenticeships are a valuable  resource  an affordable way to upskill  my team and grow my own engineers  they are facilitating our goal to punch  above our weight in the  market and create opportunities for our  team to grow as the business grows  i also found it creates loyalty within  the team  and we get longevity of employment  within  within the guys that work for us we we  don't have a high turnover staff at all  so i think i've spoken long enough now  and i'll happily hand back to our host  but i just want to  thank you for the opportunity to tell  you how 